A||||5||kempo||? about 3800 series swap||||5||
Z||000000||kempo||07-23-2001||09:18 PM||||OK- After a ride in Jason's 3800 supercharged ride, Tom went nuts.  He's added another item to his wishlist.  We're hunting down information on the engine and have found that we can get a brand spaking new one around here, with the blower, pullies, intake, and everything else with the engine for about $3,300.  Jason, you told me that the kit was about $1600... where can I attain this kit and what additional costs should be expected?  Also, what kind of transmission (manual, of course) should be used to handle the power?  Total, how much should he be looking to spend?  I've heard that you should take the cost of what you think it will be and double it.  How long will this swap take?  Any information is useful.  <BR>Unfortunately I will not be able to attend the Maple Grove event, so you guys must take pictures for me!!  Thanks!<P>-Kemp||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||07-23-2001||09:36 PM||||Have fun with the manual transmission.  Most 3800 SC have a t460E transmission.  You'll need an ECM and wiring harness for the conversion and I've heard that they are $1500.  ACE in Colorado makes wiring harnesses and The Fiero Shop in Toroto makes them.||||reg||1
Z||000002||West Coast Fiero||07-23-2001||10:10 PM|||| <A HREF="http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest/WCFpage01.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://clubs.hemmings.com/fieroswest/WCFpage01.htm</A> <P> here is a link to a 3800 we are presently doing, you may find it informative<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||NOS3800||07-23-2001||11:12 PM||||OLD LAr is mis-informed. Supercharged 3800's come with the 4T65E trans, it is important to know this cause the 4T60 will not hold up to the rigors of this motor. The 97 non SC 3800's came with the 4T60E, then in 98 they went to the 65 also.<BR>A wiring harness can be done for alot less then 1500. 300-500 is the norm. Also, the computer is only 100 bucks from a scrap yard. Usually you get this with the motor. You can get a used motor, trans, and ecm for 2200-3500 depending on the mileage. <BR>BTW, my brothers SC 3800 runs 13.3 in the quarter with the 4T65E tranny, so don't go with the manual just because you think it is faster. The fastest I have heard a manual tranny SC 3800 run is 13.7.<P><P>------------------<BR>Purple 1988 GT<BR>NOS injected 3800 Series II V6<BR>Best ET(75 shot)-13.58@99.08 mph<BR>w/o NOS 14.86@92.06mph||||reg||1
Z||000004||kempo||07-24-2001||12:10 AM||||Thanks for the info.  Being a standard transmission has nothing to do with the speed, just being a mere control freak.  I'd much rather have control over what gear the car is in, and drive the car, instead of letting the car drive me.  Appreciate it.  I'm sure I'll have more questions at a later date.  Thanks!<BR>-Kemp||||reg||1
Z||000005||hugh||07-24-2001||07:11 AM||||Kemp,Check Caspers Electronics for complete new engines.Talk to John Spina.They are in Illinois.He has new engines and blowers.He is on the internet.||||reg||1
